{
  "id": "lateralized-readiness-potential",
  "term": "lateralized readiness potential",
  "definition": "The lateralized readiness potential is a neural measure used as an index of partial information transmission during choice tasks, including go/no-go tasks. In this context, its stimulus-locked and response-locked components are used to infer how processing unfolds before a response is carried out.",
